on":"What is the word for a group of sparrows?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A host of sparrows is a traditional collective noun; host also has an older sense of a large multitude.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7ded-8d04-5852660c8da3","description":"A host","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7e12-beb0-f073322f9d06","description":"A run","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-71a8-923d-c338e9af7dd3","description":"A field","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7e52-adec-ceba479712d4","description":"A charm","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7c39-9fca-1dc6a63f8850","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is Kymatology the study of?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Kymatology comes from the Greek kyma, meaning wave; the field also applies to motions in sound and other physical systems.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-75ea-a912-bd88f5a2426a","description":"waves or wave motions","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7158-bfc4-117e4076c074","description":"weather","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7e58-b6ad-42bf7099e285","description":"Tibet","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-73fa-a3f6-0c90048ac33e","description":"mental processes in living creatures","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-74de-9be5-ecf3cc0850b0","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the name of Earth\'s rigid outer shell, made up of the crust and uppermost mantle?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"The lithosphere is Earth\'s rigid outer shell, about 100 km thick, split into tectonic plates.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7c3f-b9b2-83a6cd1210c0","description":"Lithosphere","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-71b5-bbd6-121ec6248fb5","description":"Atmosphere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-79cb-942b-10f77b176ded","description":"Hydrosphere","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-75d8-be98-8e93172f636