own as?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Tiercel comes from a word meaning \u201cthird,\u201d traditionally explained by the male being about one-third smaller than the female.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7451-9930-f41f7b54caad","description":"A Tiercel","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-71b4-9755-7f44d55def8a","description":"A Jack","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-733a-a035-0b30a1f5c92d","description":"A Cob","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-754f-b8da-a6024ab7aa3c","description":"A Boar","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-722f-befd-235a584c8cc5","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"Which German physician identified the bacterium that causes tuberculosis in 1882?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"Koch\'s postulates set out criteria for showing that a specific microorganism causes a particular disease.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-748e-8f27-c133144a0d90","description":"Robert Koch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-74ba-9c70-0b61cf5e5801","description":"Louis Pasteur","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7b62-b9ad-fa2be94b17e5","description":"Joseph Lister","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7cdc-b217-75cfd62cbac1","description":"Paul Ehrlich","correct_answer":false}]},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7d69-b45d-ebf1e3114c24","locale":"en-US","category":"01a21312-b489-7df1-b0c8-10e72868dcc8","question":"What is the word for a group of nightingales?","difficulty":3,"explanation":"A watch is the traditional collective noun for nightingales, one of many whimsical English names for groups of birds.","alternatives":[{"id":"01a218f9-3726-741f-8720-be180d37c333","description":"A watch","correct_answer":true},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7fa6-bcc1-22e4c53f3944","description":"A charm","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-704e-8829-aef79e11793a","description":"A rag","correct_answer":false},{"id":"01a218f9-3726-7428-b506-5fd94d236d8e","description":"An exaltat